286	 * safe-fallback producer applyVerdict uses (co-processor/index.ts:416) — so the
287	 * block message never diverges from the canonical block path. Escalate-only: it
288	 * can only make the gate STRICTER. Product-scoped / fail-closed: a null
289	 * product_id or a null outcome never escalates.
290	 *
291	 * FLAG-OFF ⇒ byte-identical to today: zero new work runs (NO DB read) and the
292	 * chained-in `current` {content, decision, modified} is returned unchanged.
293	 * NEVER throws into the response path — on any error it returns the unmodified
294	 * `current` plus an audit note. The counter is incremented ONLY on a real
295	 * escalation.
296	 */
